# Need the help of the chi-square test...

=== layout: bookend

# Key Takeaways

@body

- Hardy-Weinberg provides a population-genetic baseline.
- Its assumptions describe mating, population size, and gene changes.
- Compare observations with the appropriate expectation.
- Check allele changes and genotype proportions separately.

